{
  "$comment": "Apelles retake / edit-decision eval — the task set. A task is data (D-378, mirroring D-035's eval/tasks.json vocabulary: id / description / goal.checks[].metric with max|min / gates[]). The scorer is crates/apelles-speech/tests/retake_eval.rs and calls the REAL detect_retakes. Paths are relative to the repo root. `params` overrides RetakeParams (absent = default). `expect` is pinned: a task that stops matching it fails the run, so neither a fix nor a regression can land silently. Metric definitions and the labelling rules: eval/retake/README.md.",
  "$goal_rationale": "The limits are the GOAL, not today. cut_precision 1.0 and the two gates at 0.0 are D-318's one-directional rule: everything proposed for deletion must exist in what survives. retake_recall 0.5 / group_recall 0.6 are deliberately modest floors chosen so that (a) a null detector fails them outright, which is this harness's whole point, and (b) they do not demand recall the whole-utterance take model cannot express (docs/notes/retake-detection.md §2's honest limit). keeper_agreement 1.0 applies only to groups the labels marked keeper_confidence: high.",
  "tasks": [
    {
      "id": "bad/b246_tail_repeat",
      "description": "CONTROL, expected to FAIL. B-246's shape: a single-utterance take whose tail repeats the next delivery while its head is a complete unique clause. The only correct cut is the free-standing repeat; the detector cuts the long one instead.",
      "input": {
        "transcript": "eval/retake/bad_examples/b246_tail_repeat.transcript.json",
        "labels": "eval/retake/bad_examples/b246_tail_repeat.labels.json"
      },
      "goal": {
        "checks": [
          { "id": "precision", "metric": "cut_precision", "min": 1.0 },
          { "id": "recall", "metric": "retake_recall", "min": 1.0 },
          { "id": "groups", "metric": "group_recall", "min": 1.0 },
          { "id": "keeper", "metric": "keeper_agreement", "min": 1.0 }
        ]
      },
      "gates": [
        { "metric": "over_cut_secs", "max": 0.0 },
        { "metric": "protected_secs_cut", "max": 0.0 }
      ],
      "expect": "fail"
    },
    {
      "id": "bad/verbatim_retake",
      "description": "CONTROL, expected to pass. A genuine verbatim retake that MUST be cut — the case a detector cannot satisfy by proposing nothing.",
      "input": {
        "transcript": "eval/retake/bad_examples/verbatim_retake.transcript.json",
        "labels": "eval/retake/bad_examples/verbatim_retake.labels.json"
      },
      "goal": {
        "checks": [
          { "id": "precision", "metric": "cut_precision", "min": 1.0 },
          { "id": "recall", "metric": "retake_recall", "min": 0.8 },
          { "id": "groups", "metric": "group_recall", "min": 1.0 },
          { "id": "keeper", "metric": "keeper_agreement", "min": 1.0 }
        ]
      },
      "gates": [
        { "metric": "over_cut_secs", "max": 0.0 },
        { "metric": "protected_secs_cut", "max": 0.0 }
      ],
      "expect": "pass"
    },
    {
      "id": "bad/glued_anchor_unique_head",
      "description": "CONTROL, expected to FAIL since D-386, on recall only (over-cut 0.00 s). D-366 / B-238's shape: a unique setup line immediately before a genuine repeat, which a speculatively glued anchor would carry into the cut. D-366's anchor guard still keeps the setup line out; what changed is that the remaining take says 'the trick behind used' where the keeper says 'the trick being used' (the ASR mishearing in C038's real run, which this control copies), and the detector now proposes a take only when the keeper holds its every content word (the coverage gate's content rule, which cannot hear). So nothing is proposed. Fails against pre-D-366 code on over-cut instead.",
      "input": {
        "transcript": "eval/retake/bad_examples/glued_anchor_unique_head.transcript.json",
        "labels": "eval/retake/bad_examples/glued_anchor_unique_head.labels.json"
      },
      "goal": {
        "checks": [
          { "id": "precision", "metric": "cut_precision", "min": 1.0 },
          { "id": "recall", "metric": "retake_recall", "min": 0.8 },
          { "id": "groups", "metric": "group_recall", "min": 1.0 },
          { "id": "keeper", "metric": "keeper_agreement", "min": 1.0 }
        ]
      },
      "gates": [
        { "metric": "over_cut_secs", "max": 0.0 },
        { "metric": "protected_secs_cut", "max": 0.0 }
      ],
      "expect": "fail"
    },
    {
      "id": "bad/whisper_thank_you_hallucination",
      "description": "CONTROL, expected to pass. Whisper's two verbatim 'Thank you.' phantoms on room tone, 27.3 s apart at similarity 1.000. Nothing may be proposed — min_words: 3 is the only thing stopping it.",
      "input": {
        "transcript": "eval/retake/bad_examples/whisper_thank_you_hallucination.transcript.json",
        "labels": "eval/retake/bad_examples/whisper_thank_you_hallucination.labels.json"
      },
      "goal": {
        "checks": [
          { "id": "nothing", "metric": "proposed_secs", "max": 0.0, "slack": 3.0 }
